Subject: Keep the front-buffer usage bit well-defined on 32-bit targets

NDK r28 uses the same ULL literal. The r27 UL literal shifts a 32-bit
unsigned long by 32 and is rejected by upstream Clang 21.

--- a/usr/include/android/hardware_buffer.h
+++ b/usr/include/android/hardware_buffer.h
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
      * COMPOSER_OVERLAY, the system will try to prioritize the buffer receiving
      * an overlay plane & avoid caching it in intermediate composition buffers.
      */
-    AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_BUFFER = 1UL << 32,
+    AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_FRONT_BUFFER = 1ULL << 32,
 
     AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_VENDOR_0  = 1ULL << 28,
     AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_VENDOR_1  = 1ULL << 29,
